# Let the four packages that ship install scripts actually run them. On this project
# those scripts ARE the native builds, so without this npm 12 and newer install a tree
# with no .node files and the service dies on require(). Committed rather than typed on
# each Pi because CI runs `npm ci` too. Bare names match any version, so a dependency
# bump never invalidates it. Why, and what npm does on each version: docs/pi-install-prerequisites.md
#
# ⚠️ This file is COMMITTED to a public repo. Never add a registry URL, _authToken or
# any other credential here — that is what ~/.npmrc is for.
allow-scripts=better-sqlite3,socketcan,spi-device,usocket
